  "markscheme": {
    "html": "<section class=\"markscheme-part\" data-label=\"5a\"><p><strong>5a</strong></p><p></p>\n<p>The restoring force that acts on the buoy is proportional to its displacement and it points in the opposite direction.</p>\n<p></p></section><section class=\"markscheme-part\" data-label=\"5b\"><p><strong>5b</strong></p><p></p>\n<p>Since the restoring force that acts on the buoy is proportional to the displacement, <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"1.7 = k(15)\"></span>, so <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"k \\approx 0.113\"></span></p>\n<p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"F_{max} = (0.113)(28) \\approx 3.164\"></span> N</p>\n<p><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"a_{max} = \\frac{3.164}{0.42} \\approx 7.5\"></span> m s<span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"^{-2}\"></span></p>\n<p></p></section><section class=\"markscheme-part\" data-label=\"5c\"><p><strong>5c</strong></p><p> </p>\n<p>\n<figure data-asset-id=\"fig_03\"><img alt=\"Source markscheme diagram 3\" src=\"asset:fig_03\"/></figure>\n</p>\n<p> </p></section><section class=\"markscheme-part\" data-label=\"5d\"><p><strong>5d</strong></p><p></p>\n<p>Distance travelled by the buoy during half of an oscillation is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"0.56\"></span> m</p>\n<p>Time it takes for the buoy to travel this distance: <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"t = \\frac{0.56}{0.47} \\approx 1.19\"></span> s</p>\n<p>Therefore the period of the oscillations is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"2.38\"></span> s and the frequency is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\frac{1}{2.38} \\approx 0.42\"></span> Hz</p>\n<p></p></section>"
  },
  "paper": "paper_2",
  "question": {
    "html": "<p>A vertical, cylindrical buoy of mass <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"0.42\"></span> kg is floating in the ocean. The horizontal line on the buoy shows the level of the water when the buoy is at rest. When a sea bird sits on the buoy, the buoy is displaced vertically downwards by a distance of <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"28\"></span> cm. At <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"t = 0\"></span> the bird flies away from the buoy.</p>\n\n<figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure>\n\n<p>a. Outline why the buoy oscillates with simple harmonic motion (SHM) when the bird flies away.</p>\n<p>  [1]</p>\n<p>When the horizontal line on the buoy is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"15\"></span> cm above the water surface, the restoring force that acts on the buoy is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"1.7\"></span> N.</p>\n<p>b. Calculate the maximum acceleration of the buoy.</p>\n<p>   [2]</p>\n<p>c. Sketch how the kinetic energy of the buoy varies with time during one complete oscillation.</p>\n\n<figure data-asset-id=\"fig_02\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 2\" src=\"asset:fig_02\"/></figure>\n\n<p>   [2]</p>\n<p></p>\n<p>d. The average speed of the buoy during half of an oscillation is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"0.47\"></span> m s<span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"^{-1}\"></span>. Calculate the frequency of the buoy’s oscillations.</p>\n<p>   [2]</p>"
  },
